<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Château Clique</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Château Clique was the name given to the small group of wealthy English-speaking merchants, officials and seigneurs who dominated the appointed councils of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> in the early 19th century. Named after the governor's residence, the Château Saint-Louis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> City, it opposed the French-Canadian majority in the elected assembly led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-joseph-papineau">Louis-Joseph Papineau</a>. The conflict contributed to the rebellions of 1837–1838.</p></div>
